{"id":1357,"date":"2020-11-26T19:09:34","date_gmt":"2020-11-27T03:09:34","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/?post_type=lesson&#038;p=1357"},"modified":"2023-08-21T08:40:50","modified_gmt":"2023-08-21T15:40:50","slug":"program-the-gorilla-bot","status":"publish","type":"lesson","link":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/lesson\/program-the-gorilla-bot\/","title":{"rendered":"Program the Gorilla Bot"},"content":{"rendered":"<div class=\"wpb-content-wrapper\"><p>[vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a22163e2df6c\" name=\"6a22163e2df6c\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 1<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>What it does<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]The Gorilla Bot can move forward, backward, right, and left, and it can also speed up or down. You get to use a remote control again!<\/p>\n<p>This is the Gorilla Bot&#8217;s pseudocode:<\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>If up is pressed on the remote control, move forward.<\/li>\n<li>Else, if down is pressed, move backward.<\/li>\n<li>Else, if\u00a0right is pressed, move right.<\/li>\n<li>Else, if\u00a0left is pressed, move left.<\/li>\n<li>If F1 is pressed, speed up.<\/li>\n<li>Else, if\u00a0F2 is pressed slow down.<\/li>\n<li>Else, if\u00a0C is pressed, move forward at full speed.<\/li>\n<li>Else, stop.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a22163e2e082\" name=\"6a22163e2e082\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 2<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Setup<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]The first thing you need to do is include the Smart Inventor library. Next, in void setup(), include your motors and remote control, because you kind of need those for your Gorilla Bot to move.<\/p>\n<pre class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"cpp\">#include &lt;SmartInventor.h&gt;\r\n \r\nvoid setup() {\r\n  SmartInventor.DCMotorUse();\r\n  SmartInventor.TVRemoconUse();\r\n}<\/pre>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a22163e2e0ea\" name=\"6a22163e2e0ea\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 3<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>LEDs<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]Just like the Trailer Bot, you can program your LEDs to display how fast or slow your Gorilla Bot is moving! First, set up a speed variable underneath the Smart Inventor library, and then set variables for the LEDs so they can display speed later on. In void setup(), use pinMode to set the LEDs as outputs and use digitalWrite to make sure pins 13 through 16 are on.<\/p>\n<pre class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"cpp\">#include &lt;SmartInventor.h&gt;\r\n \r\nint speed = 50;\r\n\r\nint speedMeterL = 13;\r\nint speedMeterR = 16;\r\n \r\nvoid setup() {\r\n  SmartInventor.DCMotorUse();\r\n  SmartInventor.TVRemoconUse();\r\n \r\n  pinMode(11, OUTPUT);\r\n  pinMode(12, OUTPUT);\r\n  pinMode(13, OUTPUT);\r\n  pinMode(14, OUTPUT);\r\n  pinMode(15, OUTPUT);\r\n  pinMode(16, OUTPUT);\r\n  pinMode(17, OUTPUT);\r\n  pinMode(18, OUTPUT);\r\n \r\n  digitalWrite(13, HIGH);\r\n  digitalWrite(14, HIGH);\r\n  digitalWrite(15, HIGH);\r\n  digitalWrite(16, HIGH);\r\n}<\/pre>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a22163e2e141\" name=\"6a22163e2e141\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 4<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Add remote control data<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]Create a\u00a0variable\u00a0to read the\u00a0remote control\u00a0and store information about the last button that was pressed. You want this information to be read continuously, so make sure it&#8217;s in\u00a0void loop().<\/p>\n<pre class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"cpp\">#include &lt;SmartInventor.h&gt;\r\n \r\nint speed = 50;\r\n\r\nint speedMeterL = 13;\r\nint speedMeterR = 16;\r\n \r\nvoid setup() {\r\n  SmartInventor.DCMotorUse();\r\n  SmartInventor.TVRemoconUse();\r\n \r\n  pinMode(11, OUTPUT);\r\n  pinMode(12, OUTPUT);\r\n  pinMode(13, OUTPUT);\r\n  pinMode(14, OUTPUT);\r\n  pinMode(15, OUTPUT);\r\n  pinMode(16, OUTPUT);\r\n  pinMode(17, OUTPUT);\r\n  pinMode(18, OUTPUT);\r\n \r\n  digitalWrite(13, HIGH);\r\n  digitalWrite(14, HIGH);\r\n  digitalWrite(15, HIGH);\r\n  digitalWrite(16, HIGH);\r\n}\r\n \r\nvoid loop() {\r\n  int keyData = SmartInventor.TVRemoconData();\r\n}<\/pre>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a22163e2e192\" name=\"6a22163e2e192\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 5<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Add buttons<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]Next up: the main section of the code! Use if, else if, and else statements to check if any of the remote control&#8217;s buttons have been pressed. If they have, the motors will turn in that direction. For example, if you press the up button, the motors will spin in the same direction to move forward.<\/p>\n<pre class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"cpp\">void loop() {\r\n  int keyData = SmartInventor.TVRemoconData();\r\n \r\n  if(keyData == KEY_U)\r\n  {\r\n    SmartInventor.DCMotor(M1, CCW, speed);\r\n    SmartInventor.DCMotor(M2, CW, speed);\r\n  }\r\n  else if(keyData == KEY_L)\r\n  {\r\n    SmartInventor.DCMotor(M1, CCW, speed);\r\n    SmartInventor.DCMotor(M2, CCW, speed);\r\n  }\r\n  else if(keyData == KEY_R)\r\n  {\r\n    SmartInventor.DCMotor(M1, CW, speed);\r\n    SmartInventor.DCMotor(M2, CW, speed);\r\n  }\r\n  else if(keyData == KEY_D)\r\n  {\r\n    SmartInventor.DCMotor(M1, CW, speed);\r\n    SmartInventor.DCMotor(M2, CCW, speed);\r\n  }\r\n}<\/pre>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a22163e2e1df\" name=\"6a22163e2e1df\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 6<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Go faster<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]If you want to add more buttons, you can just use more else if statements in your code. For example, adding the center button on the remote control (KEY_C in your code) will make your Gorilla Bot move at full speed!<\/p>\n<pre class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"cpp\">void loop() {\r\n  int keyData = SmartInventor.TVRemoconData();\r\n \r\n  if(keyData == KEY_U)\r\n  {\r\n    SmartInventor.DCMotor(M1, CCW, speed);\r\n    SmartInventor.DCMotor(M2, CW, speed);\r\n  }\r\n  else if(keyData == KEY_L)\r\n  {\r\n    SmartInventor.DCMotor(M1, CCW, speed);\r\n    SmartInventor.DCMotor(M2, CCW, speed);\r\n  }\r\n  else if(keyData == KEY_R)\r\n  {\r\n    SmartInventor.DCMotor(M1, CW, speed);\r\n    SmartInventor.DCMotor(M2, CW, speed);\r\n  }\r\n  else if(keyData == KEY_D)\r\n  {\r\n    SmartInventor.DCMotor(M1, CW, speed);\r\n    SmartInventor.DCMotor(M2, CCW, speed);\r\n  }\r\n  else if(keyData == KEY_C)\r\n  {\r\n    SmartInventor.DCMotor(M1, CCW, 127);\r\n    SmartInventor.DCMotor(M2, CW, 127);\r\n  }\r\n}<\/pre>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a22163e2e22d\" name=\"6a22163e2e22d\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 7<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Slow down<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]What if you want your Gorilla Bot to slow down? You can add an else statement to the end of your code to bring your Gorilla Bot to a slow stop when no buttons are pressed.<\/p>\n<pre class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"cpp\">void loop() {\r\n  int keyData = SmartInventor.TVRemoconData();\r\n \r\n  if(keyData == KEY_U)\r\n  {\r\n    SmartInventor.DCMotor(M1, CCW, speed);\r\n    SmartInventor.DCMotor(M2, CW, speed);\r\n  }\r\n  else if(keyData == KEY_L)\r\n  {\r\n    SmartInventor.DCMotor(M1, CCW, speed);\r\n    SmartInventor.DCMotor(M2, CCW, speed);\r\n  }\r\n  else if(keyData == KEY_R)\r\n  {\r\n    SmartInventor.DCMotor(M1, CW, speed);\r\n    SmartInventor.DCMotor(M2, CW, speed);\r\n  }\r\n  else if(keyData == KEY_D)\r\n  {\r\n    SmartInventor.DCMotor(M1, CW, speed);\r\n    SmartInventor.DCMotor(M2, CCW, speed);\r\n  }\r\n  else if(keyData == KEY_C)\r\n  {\r\n    SmartInventor.DCMotor(M1, CCW, 127);\r\n    SmartInventor.DCMotor(M2, CW, 127);\r\n  }\r\n  else\r\n  {\r\n    SmartInventor.DCMotor(M1, LOOSE, 0);\r\n    SmartInventor.DCMotor(M2, LOOSE, 0);\r\n  }\r\n}<\/pre>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a22163e2e2ae\" name=\"6a22163e2e2ae\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 8<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Change the speed!<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]Your Gorilla Bot has more speeds besides full speed and slow stop. To include your remote control&#8217;s F1 and F2 buttons, which will speed up or slow down the motors, use if and else if statements after your code for the other buttons. You should also add in short delays so you have time to let go of the remote control&#8217;s button before it changes again.<\/p>\n<pre class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"cpp\">void loop() {\r\n  int keyData = SmartInventor.TVRemoconData();\r\n \r\n  if(keyData == KEY_U)\r\n  {\r\n    SmartInventor.DCMotor(M1, CCW, speed);\r\n    SmartInventor.DCMotor(M2, CW, speed);\r\n  }\r\n  else if(keyData == KEY_L)\r\n  {\r\n    SmartInventor.DCMotor(M1, CCW, speed);\r\n    SmartInventor.DCMotor(M2, CCW, speed);\r\n  }\r\n  else if(keyData == KEY_R)\r\n  {\r\n    SmartInventor.DCMotor(M1, CW, speed);\r\n    SmartInventor.DCMotor(M2, CW, speed);\r\n  }\r\n  else if(keyData == KEY_D)\r\n  {\r\n    SmartInventor.DCMotor(M1, CW, speed);\r\n    SmartInventor.DCMotor(M2, CCW, speed);\r\n  }\r\n  else if(keyData == KEY_C)\r\n  {\r\n    SmartInventor.DCMotor(M1, CCW, 127);\r\n    SmartInventor.DCMotor(M2, CW, 127);\r\n  }\r\n  else\r\n  {\r\n    SmartInventor.DCMotor(M1, LOOSE, 0);\r\n    SmartInventor.DCMotor(M2, LOOSE, 0);\r\n  }\r\n \r\n  if(keyData == KEY_F1)\r\n  {\r\n    if(speed &lt; 90)\r\n    {\r\n      speed = speed + 20;\r\n \r\n      delay(150);\r\n    }\r\n  }\r\n  else if(keyData == KEY_F2)\r\n  {\r\n    if(speed &gt; 30)\r\n    {\r\n      speed = speed - 20;\r\n \r\n      delay(150);\r\n    }\r\n  }\r\n}<\/pre>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a22163e2e313\" name=\"6a22163e2e313\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 9<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Add LEDs and sound<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]The middle LEDs (13-16) on your Smart Inventor Board can be programmed to display your Gorilla Bot&#8217;s speed. Every time that the speed increases or decreases, two LEDs will turn on or off. You can also add a beep in so you can hear when your Gorilla Bot&#8217;s speed changes.<\/p>\n<pre class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"cpp\">void loop() {\r\n  int keyData = SmartInventor.TVRemoconData();\r\n \r\n  if(keyData == KEY_U)\r\n  {\r\n    SmartInventor.DCMotor(M1, CCW, speed);\r\n    SmartInventor.DCMotor(M2, CW, speed);\r\n  }\r\n  else if(keyData == KEY_L)\r\n  {\r\n    SmartInventor.DCMotor(M1, CCW, speed);\r\n    SmartInventor.DCMotor(M2, CCW, speed);\r\n  }\r\n  else if(keyData == KEY_R)\r\n  {\r\n    SmartInventor.DCMotor(M1, CW, speed);\r\n    SmartInventor.DCMotor(M2, CW, speed);\r\n  }\r\n  else if(keyData == KEY_D)\r\n  {\r\n    SmartInventor.DCMotor(M1, CW, speed);\r\n    SmartInventor.DCMotor(M2, CCW, speed);\r\n  }\r\n  else if(keyData == KEY_C)\r\n  {\r\n    SmartInventor.DCMotor(M1, CCW, 127);\r\n    SmartInventor.DCMotor(M2, CW, 127);\r\n  }\r\n  else\r\n  {\r\n    SmartInventor.DCMotor(M1, LOOSE, 0);\r\n    SmartInventor.DCMotor(M2, LOOSE, 0);\r\n  }\r\n \r\n  if(keyData == KEY_F1)\r\n  {\r\n    if(speed &lt; 90)\r\n    {\r\n      speed = speed + 20;\r\n         \/\/ light up two more LEDs \r\n      speedMeterL = speedMeterL - 1; \r\n      speedMeterR = speedMeterR + 1; \r\n \r\n      digitalWrite(speedMeterL, HIGH);\r\n      digitalWrite(speedMeterR, HIGH);\r\n \r\n      SmartInventor.Buzz(1160, 12);\r\n \r\n      delay(150);\r\n    }\r\n  }\r\n  else if(keyData == KEY_F2)\r\n  {\r\n    if(speed &gt; 30)\r\n    {\r\n      speed = speed - 20;\r\n         \/\/ turn off the outer two leds\r\n      digitalWrite(speedMeterL, LOW); \r\n      digitalWrite(speedMeterR, LOW);\r\n \r\n      speedMeterL = speedMeterL + 1;\r\n      speedMeterR = speedMeterR - 1;\r\n \r\n      SmartInventor.Buzz(1160, 12);\r\n \r\n      delay(150);\r\n    }\r\n  }\r\n}<\/pre>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a22163e2e364\" name=\"6a22163e2e364\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 10<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Final code<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]Your final code should look something like this:<\/p>\n<pre class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"cpp\">#include &lt;SmartInventor.h&gt; \r\n\r\nint speed = 50; \r\n\r\nint speedMeterL = 13;\r\nint speedMeterR = 16; \r\n\r\nvoid setup() {  \r\n    SmartInventor.DCMotorUse();  \r\n    SmartInventor.TVRemoconUse();   \r\n\r\n    pinMode(11, OUTPUT);  \r\n    pinMode(12, OUTPUT);  \r\n    pinMode(13, OUTPUT);  \r\n    pinMode(14, OUTPUT);  \r\n    pinMode(15, OUTPUT);  \r\n    pinMode(16, OUTPUT);  \r\n    pinMode(17, OUTPUT);  \r\n    pinMode(18, OUTPUT);   \r\n\r\n    digitalWrite(13, HIGH);  \r\n    digitalWrite(14, HIGH);  \r\n    digitalWrite(15, HIGH);  \r\n    digitalWrite(16, HIGH);\r\n} \r\n\r\nvoid loop() {  \r\n    int keyData = SmartInventor.TVRemoconData();   \r\n\r\n    if(keyData == KEY_U)  \r\n    {    \r\n        SmartInventor.DCMotor(M1, CCW, speed);    \r\n        SmartInventor.DCMotor(M2, CW, speed);  \r\n    }  \r\n    else if(keyData == KEY_L)  \r\n    {    \r\n        SmartInventor.DCMotor(M1, CCW, speed);    \r\n        SmartInventor.DCMotor(M2, CCW, speed);  \r\n    }  \r\n    else if(keyData == KEY_R)  \r\n    {    \r\n        SmartInventor.DCMotor(M1, CW, speed);    \r\n        SmartInventor.DCMotor(M2, CW, speed);  \r\n    }  \r\n    else if(keyData == KEY_D)  \r\n    {    \r\n        SmartInventor.DCMotor(M1, CW, speed);    \r\n        SmartInventor.DCMotor(M2, CCW, speed);  \r\n    }  \r\n    else if(keyData == KEY_C)  \r\n    {    \r\n        SmartInventor.DCMotor(M1, CCW, 127);    \r\n        SmartInventor.DCMotor(M2, CW, 127);  \r\n    }  \r\n    else  \r\n    {    \r\n        SmartInventor.DCMotor(M1, LOOSE, 0);    \r\n        SmartInventor.DCMotor(M2, LOOSE, 0);  \r\n    }   \r\n\r\n    if(keyData == KEY_F1)  \r\n    {    \r\n        if(speed &lt; 90)    \r\n        {      \r\n            speed = speed + 20;                \r\n        \r\n            speedMeterL = speedMeterL - 1;   \/\/ light up two more LEDs    \r\n            speedMeterR = speedMeterR + 1;        \r\n\r\n            digitalWrite(speedMeterL, HIGH);      \r\n            digitalWrite(speedMeterR, HIGH);       \r\n\r\n            SmartInventor.Buzz(1160, 12);       \r\n\r\n            delay(150);    \r\n        }  \r\n    }  \r\n    else if(keyData == KEY_F2)  \r\n    {\r\n        if(speed &gt; 30)    \r\n        {      \r\n            speed = speed - 20;         \/\/ turn off the outer two leds      \r\n\r\n            digitalWrite(speedMeterL, LOW);       \r\n            digitalWrite(speedMeterR, LOW);       \r\n\r\n            speedMeterL = speedMeterL + 1;      \r\n            speedMeterR = speedMeterR - 1;       \r\n\r\n            SmartInventor.Buzz(1160, 12);       \r\n\r\n            delay(150);    \r\n        }  \r\n    }\r\n}<\/pre>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a22163e2e3d3\" name=\"6a22163e2e3d3\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 11<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Video<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]Still not sure about the lesson or want to make sure your program is correct? Watch the video![\/vc_column_text][vc_video link=&#8221;https:\/\/www.youtube.com\/watch?v=XzoLbdwEQwE&#8221; align=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row]<\/p>\n<\/div>","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"[vc_row][vc_column] Step 12 What it does [vc_column_text]The Gorilla Bot can move forward, backward, right, and left, and it can also speed up or down. You get to use a remote&nbsp;<a href=\"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/lesson\/program-the-gorilla-bot\/\">&hellip;<\/a>","protected":false},"featured_media":1744,"template":"","meta":{"_initial_content":"","_new_post":false,"_quiz_has_questions":true,"_lesson_complexity":"","_lesson_length":10,"_lesson_course":802,"_lesson_preview":"preview"},"lesson-category":[1814,1760,1777,1815,1808,1793,1913,1915,423,626,1533,1438,853,144,59,171,63],"lesson-tag":[2163,2218,2173,2200,2120,2122,2172,2171,2189],"class_list":["post-1357","lesson","type-lesson","status-publish","has-post-thumbnail","hentry","lesson-tag-arduino","lesson-tag-computer-science","lesson-tag-electronics","lesson-tag-gorilla-bot","lesson-tag-led","lesson-tag-programming","lesson-tag-robotics","lesson-tag-rokit-smart","lesson-tag-sensors","module-gorilla","post","odd"],"_links":{"self":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons\/1357","targetHints":{"allow":["GET"]}}],"collection":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons"}],"about":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/types\/lesson"}],"version-history":[{"count":2,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons\/1357\/revisions"}],"predecessor-version":[{"id":1525,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons\/1357\/revisions\/1525"}],"wp:featuredmedia":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media\/1744"}],"wp:attachment":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media?parent=1357"}],"wp:term":[{"taxonomy":"lesson-category","embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lesson-category?post=1357"},{"taxonomy":"lesson-tag","embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lesson-tag?post=1357"}],"curies":[{"name":"wp","href":"https:\/\/api.w.org\/{rel}","templated":true}]}}